<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>News from Asia-Pacific - Latest headlines and news reports - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24’s coverage of political, social and geostrategic issues across Asia and the Pacific, including those affecting China, Japan, South Korea, North Korea, India, Pakistan and Australia.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/rss</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:07:09Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Nepal’s catastrophic floods were ‘warning to the world,’ PM Shah tells UN</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:580676e335c6df50e4769d973b90dabb5c319799485000543979e482e8931ca0</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:07:09Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T01:42:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260925-nepal-floods-warning-world-pm-shah-un" /><summary type="html">Nepal’s Prime Minister Balendra Shah said on Thursday that last month’s catastrophic floods were a “warning to the world” of growing climate risks in the Himalayas. He said warming was melting glaciers and permafrost and urged international support to help Nepal adapt to threats it could not face alone.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>The future of AI in their hands? Trump-Xi summit dismisses calls for global oversight</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:10e7948c4b4fb7e3536b30870df79667d5cd05a18801013995cfb53139d59224</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:07:09Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T19:05:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260924-the-future-of-ai-in-their-hands-trump-xi-summit-dismisses-calls-for-global-oversight--3fbc99bf55eb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260924-the-future-of-ai-in-their-hands-trump-xi-summit-dismisses-calls-for-global-oversight" /><summary type="html">It’s their AI world and we’re just living in it. If that's the feeling of those who suffer from AI anxiety, it may worsen watching the Chinese president’s first state visit to Washington in nine years. If there's one issue where the planet's biggest superpowers agree on, it's now’s not the time for global regulation of artificial intelligence. As they sit down to a White House dinner hours after news that OpenAI had hacked the Australian government, we’ll ask who will call to task the US tech titans at the table.</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>'Trump views US-China relations as a personal friendship: Xi views US as an adversary to be managed'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d97f0b7711a099704e3293feed9e6900d4738905df78148eb809f2b49c37591a</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:07:09Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T15:01:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/trump-views-us-china-relations-as-a-personal-friendship-xi-views-us-as-an-adversary-to-be-managed--29eaaa0e21d8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/trump-views-us-china-relations-as-a-personal-friendship-xi-views-us-as-an-adversary-to-be-managed" /><summary type="html">Erin Ogunkeye is pleased to welcome Henrietta Levin, Senior Fellow with the Freeman Chair in China Studies at the Center for Strategic and International Studies in Washington. The US remains a powerful actor in its relationship with China. But power on paper is not the same thing as leverage at the negotiating table. Levin warns that President Trump’s highly personalized approach to Xi Jinping offers Beijing opportunities that China can easily exploit. Xi does not approach the relationship in the same way. Au contraire, he sees the United States as an adversary to be managed while China pursues its domestic priorities and strategic objectives in Asia, including on Taiwan.</summary></entry><entry><title>Taiwan: Home of semiconductor giants at the centre of AI race</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2448617ba74257fe43746c2e93cfcec96a0333b71aac92d91d1fa27359d87c87</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:07:09Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T13:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20260924-taiwan-home-of-semiconductor-giants-at-the-centre-of-ai-race--f4a0e175142c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20260924-taiwan-home-of-semiconductor-giants-at-the-centre-of-ai-race" /><summary type="html">The topic of artificial intelligence looms large as Chinese President Xi Jinping begins his highly anticipated state visit to Washington. The fate of Taiwan – coveted by its larger neighbour, China – will also be on the table. It's the global leader in superconductor research and development. These powerful chips can be found in smartphones, computers, and above all in AI development. Our France 2 colleagues take a rare look inside one of Taiwan's state-of-the-art laboratories.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>Pakistan launches air strikes in Afghanistan, killing civilians, Taliban says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:400097dbd0e7279ec6eecc3c1da194c218f144627b0ecd3ca82b27fa06e39b82</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:07:09Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T08:53:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260924-pakistan-launches-air-strikes-in-afghanistan-killing-civilians-taliban-says--7caa8e352d5c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260924-pakistan-launches-air-strikes-in-afghanistan-killing-civilians-taliban-says" /><summary type="html">Pakistan launched air strikes Thursday on 10 sites in Afghanistan in what Islamabad said was a retaliation for a drone attack by Afghanistan's Taliban forces on a border post. A Taliban government spokesman denied the allegation and said Pakistan's latest strikes killed four civilians in Afghanistan's southern and eastern provinces.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>China cracks down on scam centres in neighbouring Myanmar</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4348e6ac83d3229fa0c486abb3455599bec7ebaa0e3a1132978273c6aaaf4305</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:07:09Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T11:01:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20260923-china-cracks-down-on-scam-centres-in-neighbouring-myanmar--6eaea5ec0493.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20260923-china-cracks-down-on-scam-centres-in-neighbouring-myanmar" /><summary type="html">In Southeast Asia, hundreds of thousands of people working in fraud centres are scamming people across the world. US authorities suggest the fraudsters are responsible for scams worth almost $10 billion a year against US nationals alone. Victims in Europe, the UK and China have also been targeted. Human rights groups further warn that those working in the centres are often themselves victims of human trafficking – forced to work as slaves.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>Sri Lanka: 15 convicted over Easter bombings</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b90596e1b728ba7257c19d1681b6d8540a73c1788c6cbdb4b335a399821a9692</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:07:09Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T09:36:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/sri-lanka-15-convicted-over-easter-bombings--22aa604a66ba.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/sri-lanka-15-convicted-over-easter-bombings" /><summary type="html">Sri Lanka’s 2019 Easter bombings, one of the deadliest attacks in the country’s history, killed more than 260 people. After a trial lasting nearly five years, 15 men have now been convicted over the attacks, which were inspired by the Islamic State group. All those convicted are members of Sri Lanka’s Muslim minority. Ellen Gainsford reports on their sentences.</summary></entry><entry><title>Pakistan arrests sisters of imprisoned former PM Imran Khan</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:18906bab614402ac27fa7eebf5b4bf8e315b670766b6acd922643e13fedb3231</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:07:09Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T07:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260921-sisters-of-jailed-former-pakistani-pm-imran-khan-arrested--ad35916c88df.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260921-sisters-of-jailed-former-pakistani-pm-imran-khan-arrested" /><summary type="html">The three sisters of former Pakistani prime minister Imran Khan were arrested in the province of Punjab, his Tehreek-e-Insaf party said on Monday. Khan, who was prime minister from 2018 to 2022, has been imprisoned since 2023 and was sentenced last year to 17 years on corruption charges.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>North Korea fires two ballistic missiles into the sea in latest weapons display</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:15f501db39e166528fb933dce9294429855d8245ec41faae2ff0d93872c4991f</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:07:09Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T11:40:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260920-north-korea-fires-two-ballistic-missiles-into-the-sea-in-latest-weapons-display--e0338db75d93.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260920-north-korea-fires-two-ballistic-missiles-into-the-sea-in-latest-weapons-display" /><summary type="html">North Korea fired two short-range ballistic missiles into the sea off its eastern coast on Sunday, South Korea’s military said. This came days after Pyongyang reaffirmed its status as a nuclear-armed state and rejected a UN resolution calling for an end to its nuclear activities.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Japan under pressure amid accommodation woes as Asian Games kick off</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c939d9e5851038c68a3dca83e5ba04aac81da125f2c801e929abe362126f3de0</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:07:09Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T10:02:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/japan-under-pressure-amid-accommodation-woes-as-asian-games-kick-off--c800f315db92.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/japan-under-pressure-amid-accommodation-woes-as-asian-games-kick-off" /><summary type="html">It’s the world's biggest sporting event, held every four years – the 20th edition of Asian games is starting in Japan. Organisers came under pressure even before competition began… as thousands more athletes and officials registered to take part than initially expected. Story by Charlotte Lam.</summary></entry><entry><title>AI safety: No, China will not hit the brakes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6de60110ab3b8d5fe5314b988523f66d66bdb4dc042f2a2841eca9059c0e14d2</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:07:09Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T15:40:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/access-asia/20260918-ai-safety-no-china-will-not-hit-the-brakes--a3a1637a9405.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/access-asia/20260918-ai-safety-no-china-will-not-hit-the-brakes" /><summary type="html">A spate of warnings in recent days about the dangers of AI have sparked mixed reactions: from Donald Trump dismissing the fears as a hoax, to Beijing criticising calls for the US to block its advancement as fearmongering. As President Xi Jinping heads to Washington for talks, FRANCE 24's technology correspondent Peter O'Brien explains why the two superpowers are unlikely to forge binding agreements on AI regulation.</summary><category term="Access Asia" /></entry><entry><title>India vows to protect energy security after new US tariffs over Russian oil</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fab0b8204784c763bbed7716e9ecfadaf406c11b8386f13e4e8bb566368e2c6c</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:07:09Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T18:50:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/india-vows-to-protect-energy-security-after-new-us-tariffs-over-russian-oil--8b7b9fba5796.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/india-vows-to-protect-energy-security-after-new-us-tariffs-over-russian-oil" /><summary type="html">India has warned Washington that new measures to levy tariffs over the purchase of Russian oil could impact bilateral ties, the South Asian nation's foreign ministry said on Thursday, hours after the U.S. made a ​new move to ‌punish such buyers. Earlier in the day, the U.S. House of Representatives passed a sweeping sanctions and tariff bill intended ⁠to increase economic pressure on Russia over its invasion of Ukraine. FRANCE 24's Emerald Maxwell reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Erdogan to sidestep Turkey’s constitutional term limits in early 2028 vote, adviser says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:76a62fb225687004d538676fd64fd0bf4ffe11e7ec7f1a44cde19a67953dc971</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:07:09Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T13:12:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260917-turkey-s-erdogan-to-run-in-early-2028-vote-sidestepping-constitutional-term-limit--a36ab3db2bec.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260917-turkey-s-erdogan-to-run-in-early-2028-vote-sidestepping-constitutional-term-limit" /><summary type="html">Turkish President Recep Tayyip Erdogan intends to run in an early election in 2028 in order to circumvent the constitutional term limits he would face if he serves out his full current term, a top adviser said Thursday. Under Turkey's constitution, parliament can trigger early elections given the support of 360 lawmakers, meaning the ruling AKP and its nationalist ally MHP will need support of at least 34 more lawmakers.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Hong Kong unveils first five-year plan to cement position as global financial hub</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ab443849a71fcdefa27b8e76084931b89a174195f12a4f0d124af25c95d69f86</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:07:09Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T05:54:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260916-hong-kong-unveils-first-five-year-plan-to-cement-position-as-global-financial-hub--56f27ec8290b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260916-hong-kong-unveils-first-five-year-plan-to-cement-position-as-global-financial-hub" /><summary type="html">Hong ⁠Kong leader ​John Lee on Wednesday unveiled the city's first five-year plan to boost its global position as a financial hub. The plan serves as a social and economic roadmap detailing the city-state's strategic priorities, including an aim to expand technology ties with mainland China.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>China projecting image of 'stabilising force in world politics', expert says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8ff8cc4c5f19514814e92b3367fb6427aad74b4cc3abdd24d2dd59e86e1fc2f5</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:07:09Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T21:06:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20260915-china-projecting-image-of-stabilising-force-in-world-politics-expert-says--48ed2a17448e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20260915-china-projecting-image-of-stabilising-force-in-world-politics-expert-says" /><summary type="html">Speaking with FRANCE 24's Monte Francis, Rex Li, Professor of International Relations at King's College London, says that China "is trying to promote an alternative international security order and project itself as a stabilising force in world politics", adding that while Beijing "is increasingly willing to play a more significant part in ending the conflict in the Middle East, so far we haven't seen any concrete proposals coming from China".</summary><category term="A propos" /></entry><entry><title>China projecting image of 'stabilising force in world politics', expert says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e2a7e2729af1820ee96f80fef7fdd52e9a12e09f134e2e1f652f23ffa0d9821a</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:07:09Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T21:04:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/china-projecting-image-of-stabilising-force-in-world-politics-expert-says--5cc52bcb6cf4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/china-projecting-image-of-stabilising-force-in-world-politics-expert-says" /><summary type="html">Speaking with FRANCE 24's Monte Francis, Rex Li, Professor of International Relations at King's College London, says that China "is trying to promote an alternative international security order and project itself as a stabilising force in world politics", adding that while Beijing "is increasingly willing to play a more significant part in ending the conflict in the Middle East, so far we haven't seen any concrete proposals coming from China".</summary></entry><entry><title>Viral Putin, Modi and Xi selfie at BRICS summit is AI-generated</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ef0862749703e4333fb2e479c01e1842727298fd4718ea3be58fafc3144ae870</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:07:09Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T19:49:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20260915-viral-putin-modi-and-xi-selfie-at-brics-summit-is-ai-generated--c818ffc4f677.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20260915-viral-putin-modi-and-xi-selfie-at-brics-summit-is-ai-generated" /><summary type="html">A viral selfie allegedly showing leaders including, Russian President Vladimir Putin, Chinese President Xi Jinping and Indian Prime Minister Narendra at the BRICS summit in New Delhi is AI-generated. A SynthID watermark shows it was created using OpenAI tools. Several leaders pictured, including Brazil’s Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva and Turkey’s Recep Tayyip Erdoğan, did not attend. Another AI selfie features former Iranian president Ebrahim Raisi, who died in 2024. Both images were widely shared online, including by official embassy accounts. Vedika Bahl fact-checks.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>Turkey police disperse pro-LGBTQ protesters with tear gas</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e9ea220d22d1cd76d98f1c7dd29c9866ff881f0c7fb63b458c55aa3a7a91c65c</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:07:09Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T19:54:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260914-turkey-police-disperse-pro-lgbtq-protesters-with-tear-gas--85ad9b6b4b9f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260914-turkey-police-disperse-pro-lgbtq-protesters-with-tear-gas" /><summary type="html">Turkish police fired tear gas at pro-LGBTQ demonstrators in the western city of Izmir on Monday, as activists protested a nationwide crackdown that saw dozens arrested over the weekend in a campaign authorities described as defending traditional family values.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>'What makes China work despite the pain in society?' asks analyst Dan Wang</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e5d33f89de6b1133707b67c5afd8b7277a413ac074c350709c0ffa1490b1f679</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:07:09Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T13:30:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/what-makes-china-work-despite-the-pain-in-society-asks-analyst-dan-wang--d40c2ced80a4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/what-makes-china-work-despite-the-pain-in-society-asks-analyst-dan-wang" /><summary type="html">In this edition of Perspective, FRANCE 24’s Stuart Norval speaks to Dan Wang, a China expert whose book ‘Breakneck:  China’s Quest to Engineer the Future’ is a New York Times bestseller. It takes a close look at Chinese life and draws from Wang’s own ten years of living there. Wang says the China and the US are some of the most similar people in the world, as they are both hustlers and take shortcuts.</summary><category term="Perspective" /></entry><entry><title>Climate catastrophe leaves Nepal mourning while the search for the missing continues</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:37e27908b2c9bf83f79b74bbee12b65eb87cd1026b97dfd5de9d83b117d3d0de</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:07:09Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T12:43:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20260914-climate-catastrophe-leaves-nepal-mourning-while-the-search-for-the-missing-continues--40d634ca2dd0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20260914-climate-catastrophe-leaves-nepal-mourning-while-the-search-for-the-missing-continues" /><summary type="html">The himalayan flash flood that devastated northern Nepal on August 26 was an unprecedented disaster. The death toll continues to rise, with nearly 1,400 people now confirmed dead and 5,130 still missing, including around 600 foreign nationals from 35 countries.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>Indonesia: Rescuers resume search for 129 missing after ferry capsized</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d2dadb96f5fef0ecf17515d9ab038cf1eb4d7a5f5d7cbef61d32a64a5bbf0b00</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:07:09Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T08:57:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260914-indonesia-rescuers-resume-search-for-129-missing-after-ferry-capsized--3f97e7973f03.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260914-indonesia-rescuers-resume-search-for-129-missing-after-ferry-capsized" /><summary type="html">Hundreds of Indonesian rescuers including the coast guard and the navy raced on Monday to board a passenger ship that capsized in the Java Sea over the weekend as they searched for 129 people still missing, officials said, with the confirmed death toll at six.</summary></entry><entry><title>Indonesia intensifies search for more than 120 missing after ferry capsizes in Java Sea</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:998e57b5beede5b80c3c96cd14390dd1aa64c9d36dc1b73894ceb33b4aa94fa5</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:07:09Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T06:14:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260914-indonesia-intensifies-search-missing-after-ferry-capsizes-java-sea--d6966a9b01a6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260914-indonesia-intensifies-search-missing-after-ferry-capsizes-java-sea" /><summary type="html">Indonesian rescue teams on Monday deployed specialised underwater teams and navy-operated underwater drones as the search for more than 120 people missing in the Virgo Transport 8 ferry capsizing intensified.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Turkey detains dozens in raids of bars, homes in crackdown on LGBTQ community</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e93f8b5e622ef2053aa848579336b4d6d5746a52fd8dc78db4b16807874932ee</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:07:09Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T19:41:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260913-turkey-detains-dozens-in-raids-of-bars-homes-in-crackdown-on-lgbtq-community--d3deee7e6ee0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260913-turkey-detains-dozens-in-raids-of-bars-homes-in-crackdown-on-lgbtq-community" /><summary type="html">Turkish authorities on Sunday launched raids on gay bars, nightclubs, LGBTQ association offices and activists' homes in a sweeping crackdown in several cities as part of the government's "My Family is Safe" operations, Turkey's justice minister said. More than 60 people were arrested, according to the state news agency, in raids condemned by human rights groups.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Indonesia: Second ferry disaster in five days</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c69ec432d9de0fb5ec131e3528328793906ba69f9ca2dfc32afb40b582beafbb</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:07:09Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T13:17:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/indonesia-second-ferry-disaster-in-five-days--bcdea8ab2589.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/indonesia-second-ferry-disaster-in-five-days" /><summary type="html">At least one person has died and more than 100 people remain missing after a ferry carrying 243 people sank in rough weather between the Indonesian islands of Java and Borneo. The disaster is the second major ferry accident in the region in five days, renewing concerns over safety standards, overcrowding and maintenance.</summary></entry><entry><title>BRICS summit: What came out of the New Delhi meeting</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7ac3df8e92751009b23939335832fb43a2c1580fa53d28a4dc38ae57615c6416</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:07:09Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T09:27:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/brics-summit-what-came-out-of-the-new-delhi-meeting--2d7ab6cb6280.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/brics-summit-what-came-out-of-the-new-delhi-meeting" /><summary type="html">The BRICS summit in New Delhi ended with a joint declaration calling for greater Global South influence in global governance and urging restraint in the Middle East. The gathering also served as a platform for one-to-one diplomacy, with leaders holding a series of bilateral meetings aimed at easing regional tensions. FRANCE 24's Navodita Kumari has the details.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Second life': Nepal hydropower tunnel survivor recalls ordeal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fd469b4e66c2449346cc7072667967b0fc0ad8131300f368555dbfa190e9237f</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:07:09Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T04:17:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260913-second-life-nepal-hydropower-tunnel-survivor-recalls-ordeal--bac6c1a764d8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260913-second-life-nepal-hydropower-tunnel-survivor-recalls-ordeal" /><summary type="html">Nepali hydropower worker Sanjay Sah survived in total darkness inside a tunnel flooded by the deadly flash flood that struck the China-Nepal border on August 26, drinking muddy water and praying that rescuers would find him. The survivor, who was rescued on September 4, recalls the 10 days he spent stranded.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>BRICS leaders call for 'maximum restraint' as Middle East war threatens unity</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a079cfcf3e31c40e6a4d56c11b1f67e95933e9cdfb84f8af6b0ff64bd7e5610a</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:07:09Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T06:51:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260912-brics-summit-set-to-be-dominated-by-wars-in-ukraine-and-iran--19071f618e81.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260912-brics-summit-set-to-be-dominated-by-wars-in-ukraine-and-iran" /><summary type="html">BRICS leaders meeting in New Delhi on Saturday unanimously adopted a joint declaration expressing "deep concern" over the war in the Middle East and urging maximum restraint. The statement was seen as indirect criticism of US and Israeli strikes on Iranian nuclear facilities.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Hate speech against Rohingya refugees on the rise in Malaysia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:24cb85495c4370ddfc4225fdeeed7b82d3fc07ba4c31959338393f2f08184960</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:07:09Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T14:34:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-observers/20260911-hate-speech-rohingya-refugees-rise-malaysia--dd6c980fdaa8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-observers/20260911-hate-speech-rohingya-refugees-rise-malaysia" /><summary type="html">Hostile social media content, disinformation campaigns, and a petition calling for their expulsion: in Malaysia, a wave of hate speech has been targeting Rohingya refugees, a Muslim minority driven out of Myanmar. The rising hostility has already led to the eviction of more than 100 people from a village and forced the temporary closure of schools serving refugee children.</summary><category term="The Observers" /></entry><entry><title>Nepal: Rescue efforts continue in the aftermath of a flash flooding disaster</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3ab2435ce0673ca67645a6bc31c4ea27b117af6b0aa85a0016aabe547b0c6eb3</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:07:09Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T09:41:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/reporters/20260911-nepal-rescue-efforts-continue-in-the-aftermath-of-a-flash-flooding-disaster--6bc8de0c3bb9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/reporters/20260911-nepal-rescue-efforts-continue-in-the-aftermath-of-a-flash-flooding-disaster" /><summary type="html">Two weeks after the devastating flash floods, the number of dead and missing continues to rise. At Kathmandu’s public hospital, as well as outside the military base in Bidur, hundreds of photographs of missing people have been put up. Hundreds of families come forward, hoping for news – good or bad – of one or more loved ones. A race against time is underway: helping survivors, finding those still alive and identifying the victims. Rescue teams have been carrying out repeated helicopter flights, as air access is now the only way to reach remote areas cut off from the rest of the world. Civil society has also mobilised, particularly Nepal’s Generation Z. From Kathmandu to Betrawati, FRANCE 24's reporters Alban Alvarez and Fantine Dantzer accompanied a humanitarian convoy along one of the country’s most treacherous roads.</summary><category term="Reporters" /></entry><entry><title>Putin arrives in India for BRICS summit set to be dominated by Middle East, Ukraine wars</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bb599d1ec9dce53bf8eb33ac0f3ef5ad66a4eed91a97a33ec16a2e3329a77911</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:07:09Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T02:08:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260911-putin-xi-india-brics-summit-ukraine-middle-east-wars--f89644d9206b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260911-putin-xi-india-brics-summit-ukraine-middle-east-wars" /><summary type="html">Russian President Vladimir Putin arrived in New Delhi on Friday for a two-day BRICS summit expected to focus on wars in Ukraine and the Middle East and economic challenges. Putin and Iran’s President Masoud Pezeshkian are due to meet Prime Minister Narendra Modi, while China’s Xi Jinping is also expected to hold talks.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry></feed>
